Invalidation: an infill change leaves the simplified walls alone.

Invalidating posPrepareInfill also invalidated posSimplifyPath, which
simplifies the walls. The infill doesn't change the walls, and simplifying
walls that were already simplified turned their fitted arcs into lines, so a
Print sliced again after an infill change (desktop does; the browser engine
keeps the last slice's Print) printed other walls than a fresh slice. A wall
change still redoes it (posPerimeters invalidates posSimplifyPath).

diff --git a/src/libslic3r/PrintObject.cpp b/src/libslic3r/PrintObject.cpp
index 925da0c5..3dbce142 100644
--- a/src/libslic3r/PrintObject.cpp
+++ b/src/libslic3r/PrintObject.cpp
